the iterator activates with the col2 VLAN-id fix. So the mxIpIf edits STAY in the working tree (still uncommitted). NEXT TREE: user chose mxTurboRingV2 (MAC type-fix).** Files if reverting: `app_moxa_framework/src/snmp_subagent.rs` remove L3VLANIF_ROOT/l3vlanif_rows/l3vlanif_row_count/l3vlanif_iter_handler/set_int_or_truth/register_l3vlanif_table + the register call. DUT test: `snmpwalk .605.1.1.1.1` GET live via framework (match in-master exactly incl col2=0), CLI add/remove VLAN iface → immediate walk (no reboot), IpAddress types on col7/8, empty table→No Such Object. Note col2/col5 absent-field edge → noSuchInstance (configured rows always have them). iss0 remaining after this: dhcpSrv×4 (non-L3, needs MAC helper for macBasedIp), mxTurboRingV2 (MAC type-fix, optional), mx_email (IP scalar, moxa_config_handler IPADDRESS branch). ADR linkage: applies ADR-0004 pattern, step toward ADR-0005 (Proposed iss0 end-state); no ADR mutation needed (no decision reversed).

**mxTurboRingV2 MAC-render TYPE FIX IMPLEMENTED (2026-07-28, edited, awaiting build/DUT) — NOT a Plan E migration.** Vetting reframed it: mxTurboRingV2 is already Plan D (framework GET+SET, in g_reuse_srcs) and its MAC cols are ALL **RONLY status** (`stat/turboringv2/ring/designatedMaster` `.603.3.4.2.1.1.3`; + DRC-only masterPrimaryMac/masterBackupMac). NO config MAC, NO rowStatus, NO iterator, NO MAC *set* helper. **Bug:** framework `handle_status_get` had only ASN_INTEGER + `_ =>octet_string(str)`, so a MAC (val_type 0xf4) was returned as the ASCII status string (e.g. "00:00:00:00:00:00:00" = 20 bytes) instead of 6 raw bytes (MIB `mxTrv2.mib` SYNTAX=MacAddress; mainline/in-master renders 6 bytes). **Key enabler:** `SNMP_DATA_TYPE_MAC_ADDRESS=0xf4` (ies_auto_mibs_handle.h) is DISTINCT from OCTET(0x04)/IP(0x40)/INT(0x02) and carried unchanged into `MapEntry.val_type` (mapping_reuse.c:244) → framework can branch on it. **Fix (2 files, no C):** (1) `lib_moxa_rust_snmp_agentx/src/lib.rs` +`set_octet_bytes(&[u8])` (same byte-based `MoxaAgentX_SetOctetString`, no C change). (2) `app_moxa_framework/src/snmp_subagent.rs`: `const SNMP_DATA_TYPE_MAC: c_int=0xf4`, `mac_to_bytes(s)` (first 6 colon hex groups, ignore extra — byte-identical to in-master `moxa_snmp_handle_util.c:845` loop that reads exactly 6 groups), new `0xf4` arm in `handle_status_get` → set_octet_bytes(6). Only handle_status_get (that's where the MAC entries route: is_status→handle_status_get); handle_get NOT touched (no config MAC in framework groups = surgical). Build: app_moxa_framework (+ rust chain incl lib_moxa_rust_snmp_agentx) + final; NO 3rdparty_net_snmp rebuild. **DUT test:** `snmpwalk .1.3.6.1.4.1.8691.603.3.4.2.1` designatedMaster (col .1.3) — before=`STRING:"..:..:..:..:..:..:.."` (7-group ASCII), after=`Hex-STRING: xx xx xx xx xx xx` (6 bytes); type change visible even with 00s; real MAC needs a turboRing configured (ring status table must have a row). This is a status-render type-correctness fix (low impact, matches mainline), the first use of val_type 0xf4 branching — reusable for any future MAC status col.

